    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d897">

                <pb facs="0841" n="829" xml:id="pg829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/10581: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-18T20:00:00+02:00">April 18, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>699. Department’s 325, April 14.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d897-f1"/> I have kept the
                    Russian Ambassador informed concerning our note to the Turk Government with
                    respect to trade between Turkey and the Axis and immediately following my talk
                    with the Minister for Foreign Affairs (see my 678, April 15, 6 p.m.) furnished
                    Vinogradov with a copy of our note.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
